    dict(key='22-act-5-3', kind='console', title='Act Five — Keeping it right, and the bill',
         body='FIVE. (continued)\n  THE BILL:\n    naive: checks in 9 handlers, nine places to forget one\n    guarded: one table of rules that a test can read\n    every object check needs a lookup of who owns the object\n    every refusal is a log line to keep and watch',
         narration='And the bill. [[slnc 300]] The naive store kept its checks in nine handlers, nine places to forget one. [[slnc 300]] The guarded store keeps them in one table that a test can read. [[slnc 300]] Every object check needs a lookup of who owns it. [[slnc 300]] And every refusal is a log line to keep and watch.'),
    dict(key='23-ladder', kind='bullets', title='What Does Not Work, and What Does',
         body=['Hidden links: no', 'Unguessable ids: no', 'Signed in only: no', 'A check in each handler: until one is forgotten', 'One policy, deny by default, tested: yes'],
         narration="Let's put it side by side. [[slnc 400]] Hiding links in the page does not work. [[slnc 500]] Ids that are hard to guess do not work, because ids are shared. [[slnc 500]] Checking only that someone is signed in does not work. [[slnc 500]] A check in each handler works, until one is forgotten. [[slnc 500]] One policy, that refuses by default, and a test that every route has a rule, works."),
    dict(key='24-recognise', kind='bullets', title='Where You Have Seen It',
         body=['OWASP Top 10: A01', 'OWASP API Top 10: API1 and API5', 'Bug bounty reports: IDOR, BOLA', 'deny all at the end of a config'],
         narration='You have probably met this already. [[slnc 400]] It is first in the O W A S P top ten. [[slnc 500]] It is first and fifth in the O W A S P A P I security top ten, as broken object level, and function level, authorization. [[slnc 500]] Bug bounty reports call it I D O R, or B O L A. [[slnc 500]] And security configurations that end with deny all are this lesson, written down.'),
